<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sais</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sais was an ancient Egyptian city in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a>, centre of the cult of the goddess Neith. Libyan chiefs ruled from it in the 8th century BCE, and it was the seat of the Twenty-fourth Dynasty and the capital of the Twenty-sixth, or Saite, Dynasty, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 664 to 525 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyrtaeus">Amyrtaeus</a>, sole king of the Twenty-eighth Dynasty, also came from Sais.</p></div>
